### Add Local Package Dependency via Path

Source: https://github.com/composer/composer/blob/main/doc/05-repositories.md

Configure a path repository to depend on a local package within the same repository. The URL is relative to the main composer.json file.

```json
{
    "repositories": [
        {
            "type": "path",
            "url": "../../packages/my-package"
        }
    ],
    "require": {
        "my/package": "*"
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Override Package Version with Path Repository

Source: https://github.com/composer/composer/blob/main/doc/05-repositories.md

Specify a version for a local package dependency when using a path repository, overriding any version inferred from VCS or the package's composer.json.

```json
{
    "repositories": [
        {
            "type": "path",
            "url": "../../packages/my-package",
            "options": {
                "versions": {
                    "my/package": "4.2-dev"
                }
            }
        }
    ]
}
```

--------------------------------

### Require unstable dependencies

Source: https://github.com/composer/composer/blob/main/doc/04-schema.md

Explicitly require a dependency and its stability flag when a sub-dependency requires an unstable package.

```json
{
    "require": {
        "doctrine/doctrine-fixtures-bundle": "dev-master",
        "doctrine/data-fixtures": "@dev"
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Add Packages to Dev Dependencies

Source: https://github.com/composer/composer/blob/main/doc/03-cli.md

Use the --dev option to add packages specifically to the 'require-dev' section of composer.json. These are typically development tools or testing libraries.

```shell
php composer.phar require --dev vendor/package
```

--------------------------------

### Update Specific Packages

Source: https://github.com/composer/composer/blob/main/doc/03-cli.md

To update only a select few packages, list them explicitly after the update command. This is useful for targeted dependency management.

```shell
php composer.phar update vendor/package vendor/package2
```

